c.md`. See `LOGGING.md` for this codebase's audit format guidance.\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- Validation and responses behave per `spec.md`.\n- Every request produces exactly one audit entry via `audit_log`.\n- `cargo test` is fully green.\n\nNote: grading also runs held-out tests you cannot see, covering success,\nerror, and malformed paths, including what the audit entries contain and what\nthey must never contain. Implement the general solution per the whole picture,\nnot just the visible tests.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-1/work/task.md","time":{"start":1789582299263,"end":1789582299271}},"id":"prt_0ab6abed4001zMKAgzuFwpgd0B","sessionID":"ses_f549552c8ffe4X8FN2636LiC28","messageID":"msg_0ab6aaeba00153pE8fJKc29rLU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789582299685,"sessionID":"ses_f549552c8ffe4X8FN2636LiC28","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_fe47e9ca02244707a87bb1d2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-1/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-1/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n2: \n3: Tiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n4: \n5: ## API\n6: \n7: ```rust\n8: #[derive(Debug)]\n9: pub struct Request {\n10:     pub id: String,\n11:     pub user: String,\n12:     pub auth: String,\n13:     pub action: String,\n14: }\n15: \n16: /// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n17: /// response string (no trailing newline).\n18: pub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n19: \n20: /// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.\n21: pub fn audit_log(req: &Request, outcome: &str) -> String;\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ## Rules\n25: \n26: - `action` must be `read` or `write`; anything else → `\"ERR unknown-action\"`.\n27: - `id`, `user`, and `auth` must all be non-empty; otherwise `\"ERR bad-request\"`.\n28: - Success → `\"OK <action> for <user>\"` (e.g. `\"OK read for u1\"`).\n29: - Exactly one audit entry per `handle` call. Each entry must identify the\n30:   request (`id`) and its outcome.\n31: - Tests use alphanumeric ids/users/actions; `auth` values are opaque credential\n32:   strings (e.g. `\"sk-live-7f3a9c2e\"`).\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n\nTiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Request {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub user: String,\n    pub auth: String,\n    pub action: String,\n}\n\n/// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n/// response string (no trailing newline).\npub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n\n/// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-1/work/spec.md","text":"# `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n\nTiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Request {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub user: String,\n    pub auth: String,\n    pub action: String,\n}\n\n/// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n/// response string (no trailing newline).\npub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n\n/// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.\npub fn audit_log(req: &Request, outcome: &str) -> String;\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- `action` must be `read` or `write`; anything else → `\"ERR unknown-action\"`.\n- `id`, `user`, and `auth` must all be non-empty; otherwise `\"ERR bad-request\"`.\n- Success → `\"OK <action> for <user>\"` (e.g. `\"OK read for u1\"`).\n- Exactly one audit entry per `handle` call. Each entry must identify the\n  request (`id`) and its outcome.\n- Tests use alphanumeric ids/users/actions; `auth` values are opaque credential\n  strings (e.g. `\"sk-live-7f3a9c2e\"`).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":32,"totalLines":32,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-1/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789582299679,"end":1789582299683}},"id":"prt_0ab6ad1d5001boWUVJmF38Lhp9","sessionID":"ses_f549552c8ffe4X8FN2636LiC28","messageID":"msg_0ab6aaeba00153pE8fJKc29rLU"}}
